 "text": "This was supposed to go on your walls. Hawthorne, New Jersey. Two engineers, Alfred Fielding and Mark Chavannes, heat-sealed two plastic shower curtains together. Air gets trapped inside. Tiny bubbles. Their big idea? Textured wallpaper. Nobody bought it. So they tried again. Greenhouse insulation. That flopped too. Most people would quit here. They didn't. They started a company. Sealed Air. Then a marketer on their team spotted a problem. IBM was about to ship its new 1401 computer. And computers were fragile, very fragile. The bubbles were perfect. IBM became their first big customer. Today you know it as bubble wrap, a failed wallpaper that now protects packages all over the world. Every legend has a beginning.",
